rname>Snell</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Carotid artery stent type influences duplex ultrasonography derived peak systolic velocity: findings of an in-vitro model</article-title><source>Catheter Cardiovasc Interv</source><year>2007</year><volume>70</volume><fpage>309</fpage><lpage>15</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17630677</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/ccd.21224</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Flahault</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Cadilhac</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Sample size calculation should be performed for design accuracy in diagnostic test studies</article-title><source>J Clin Epidemiol</source><year>2005</year><volume>58</volume><fpage>859</fpage><lpage>62</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16018921</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.jclinepi.2004.12.009</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bossuyt</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>Towards complete and accurate reporting of studies of diagnostic accuracy: The STARD</article-title><source>Ann Intern Med</source><year>2003</year><volume>138</volume><fpage>40</fpage><lpage>4</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12513043</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>